===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:what|tree=1}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kʷ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|what}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hwæt||what}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hwat}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hwat||what}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*kʷód||what}}, neuter form of {{m|ine-pro|*kʷós||who}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|sco|what}}, {{m|sco|whit||what}}, {{cog|frr|wat||what}}, {{cog|stq|wat||what}}, {{cog|fy|wat||what}}, {{cog|nl|wat||what}}, {{cog|nds|wat||what}}, {{cog|de|was||what}}, {{cog|da|hvad||what}}, {{cog|nb|hva||what}}, {{cog|sv|vad||what}}, {{cog|nn|kva||what}}, {{cog|is|hvað||what}}, {{cog|la|quod||what, which}}.

Its [[what#Particle|use as a particle of contradiction or objection]] in colloquial Malaysian and Singaporean Englishes is {{glossary|semantic loan|analogous}} to {{sl|en|ms|apa|nocap=1|notext=1}} and {{sl|en|yue|喎|tr=wo<sup>3</sup>|pos=etymology 2, sense 3|nocap=1|notext=1}}. It is possible that this was historically reinforced by the dated use of {{l|en|what|''what'' as a sentence-final question tag|id=tag-question}} in British English.

